$plugin->release   = '1.1.40'; // UI-CV-NO-STATUS (v1.1.35): Removed status text from toolbar — nothing shown after Stop button in student view. setStatus() silenced. // FEAT-CV-ACCENT-TOOLTIP (v1.1.27): Added accent-vs-translation clarification everywhere language is configured. Gear icon tooltip updated to explain accent-only behaviour. allowedlanguages_desc admin setting updated with bold Important note. coursesettingslangdesc teacher page updated with example (French = French accent reading English, not translation). No DB changes. // RENAME-CV-SCORM (v1.1.26): // RENAME-CV-SCORM (v1.1.26): Plugin renamed from 'AI Voiceover (Chirp HD)' to 'AI SCORM Voiceover' everywhere — pluginname lang string, all PHP file headers, install.xml comment, styles.css comment, block_aiplugin_nav registry entries, pluginConfig.ts, AIVoiceover docs page. No DB changes. // FIX-CV-CASCADE-PREFETCH (v1.1.25): // FIX-CV-CASCADE-PREFETCH (v1.1.25): Eliminated heading→paragraph silence gap. Root cause: heading audio (e.g. "Porosity", ~0.5 s) was cached by prefetchNext while the previous long paragraph played, but the paragraph AFTER the heading only started fetching when the heading STARTED playing — 0.5 s audio < 3–5 s paragraph TTS = 2–4 s silence. Fix: one-level cascade in prefetchNext — after decoding segment N, immediately fire prefetchNext(N+1, true). The isCascade guard prevents infinite chaining. Now when heading is decoded (while previous paragraph still plays), the following paragraph fetch starts in parallel and is ready before the heading even finishes. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-PREFETCH-SPEED (v1.1.24): Removed playbackRate from _playBuffer entirely — it caused chipmunk pitch shift. Speed is now 100% server-side: speakingRate is sent in every TTS XHR body. Added speed guard to prefetchNext: captures chirpSpeed at XHR send time, discards the decoded AudioBuffer if speed changed before the response arrived (stale-speed audio would play at the wrong pace). No DB changes; // FIX-CV-HEADING-GAP (v1.1.23): Eliminated gap between heading and body text. Root cause: the next segment only started fetching AFTER the current segment finished playing — for short headings (~1-2 s) the next TTS request was not ready, causing a ~3 s blank. Fix: call prefetchNext(curIdx+1) from inside fetchAndPlay right before xhr.send(), so both segments are fetched in parallel. prefetchNext already guards against double-fetching. No DB changes; // UI-CV-SPEED-PLAYBACK (v1.1.22): Speed control uses AudioBufferSourceNode.playbackRate (client-side). speakingRate via TTS API requires the server audio cache to be keyed by speed across all deployments — not guaranteed. playbackRate is 100% client-side and works immediately. Range is capped at 0.9–1.1 so pitch shift is ~1.6 semitones (imperceptible; true chipmunk starts at 1.3×+). No DB changes; // FEAT-CV-SPEAKINGRATE-FIXED (v1.1.21): Speed now works end-to-end without chipmunk. Server-side fix: speakingRate added to Zod schema in /api/moodle/chirp-tts, included in the SHA-256 cache key (so 0.9x/1.0x/1.1x get separate cache entries), and passed as speakingRate to Google TTS synthesizeSpeech. Removed playbackRate from JS entirely — audio is generated at the correct pace natively. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-SPEED-PLAYBACK (v1.1.20): Restored playbackRate for immediate speed effect. speakingRate is still sent to the TTS API for future server-side support but the external TTS server cache currently ignores it. playbackRate now applies to all playback at the limited 0.9-1.1 range so pitch shift is minimal (~1.6 semitones). No DB changes; // UI-CV-SPEED-SIMPLE (v1.1.19): Simplified speed control to three steps only (0.9×, 1.0×, 1.1×). Removed 0.75×, 1.25×, 1.5× steps — they sounded identical due to Google TTS speakingRate ceiling effects. The − button goes slower (0.9×), the + button goes faster (1.1×). No DB changes; // FEAT-CV-SPEAKINGRATE (v1.1.18): Speed control now uses Google TTS speakingRate parameter natively. Audio is generated at the correct pace by the TTS engine so pitch is preserved (no chipmunk effect). Removed AudioBufferSourceNode.playbackRate manipulation entirely. When speed is changed mid-play the prefetch cache is discarded (stale audio at old rate) and the current segment restarts from the beginning at the new rate. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-HL-MISSING (v1.1.17): Highlight now persists on cache-miss segments. Root cause: playBase64 called stopAll() inside the async decodeAudioData callback, which called clearHl() — erasing the highlight playSegAt() had already applied. Fix: replaced stopAll() with targeted BufferSource stop (mirrors cache-hit path from v1.1.11). No DB changes; // UI-CV-HL-PADDING (v1.1.16); // UI-CV-HL-PADDING (v1.1.16): Added padding:5px 10px to .chirp-hl so the blue highlight box has breathing room on all four sides. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-IMG-CAPTIONS (v1.1.15); // FIX-CV-IMG-CAPTIONS (v1.1.15): Image gallery captions no longer read aloud. Added 'caption', 'block-gallery', 'image-gallery', 'gallery-item' to SKIP_ANCESTOR_CLASS_PATTERNS — catches Rise 360 3-up photo row captions and all caption-class variants. No DB changes; // UI-CV-LABEL (v1.1.14): Toolbar label changed from 'AI Voiceover' to 'Voiceover'. No DB changes; // UI-CV-TOOLBAR-CLEAN (v1.1.13): Toolbar centred at top (left:50%+translateX(-50%)); status text removed entirely (students do not need reading progress). No DB changes; // UI-CV-NO-STUDENT-VOICE (v1.1.12): Removed voice and language dropdowns from the student toolbar. Voice and language are now admin/teacher settings only, configured in plugin options. resolvedVoice and resolvedLang are computed once at toolbar build time from M_cfg defaults, validated against the admin-allowed list, and used for all TTS fetches. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-HL-PERSIST (v1.1.11): Highlight now persists for the full duration of audio playback. Root cause: fetchAndPlay's prefetch cache-hit path called stopAll() which in turn called clearHl(), erasing the highlight that playSegAt() had just set — audio played with no visible highlight. stopAll() also wiped the entire prefetchCache, defeating the prefetch system. Fix: replaced stopAll() in the cache-hit path with a minimal inline audio-source stop that does not touch the highlight or prefetchCache. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-HL-TARGET (v1.1.10): Highlight now correctly covers the full list-item visual area. For <li><p>text</p></li> bullets, getHighlightEl() promotes the highlight target from the inner <p> up to the parent <li> so the whole bullet is tinted. Replaced outline (which bleeds outside the box model and overlaps adjacent li siblings) with inset box-shadow which stays strictly inside the element boundary. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-VOICE-STALE (v1.1.9): Discard prefetch cache on voice or language change. Previously the already-prefetched next segment (fetched with the old voice) would play in the wrong voice when a student changed voice mid-play. Now a change event listener on both dropdowns clears prefetchCache immediately, forcing a fresh fetch with the new selection. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-IMG-LABELS (v1.1.8): Image labels, hotspot text, and image captions no longer read aloud. Removed figcaption from content selector; removed labeled-graphic, marker__content, label-text from Rise fallback selector; added ancestor class-pattern blocking (SKIP_ANCESTOR_CLASS_PATTERNS + hasForbiddenAncestorClass) so text inside image components is suppressed even when the p element itself has no image-related class. cleanText now also strips figcaption and role=img children. No DB changes; // FIX-CV-LI-DUP (v1.1.7): Skip <li> elements that contain block-level children — Rise 360 renders <li><p>text</p></li> so both were selected, reading each bullet twice. // PERF-CV-PREFETCH (v1.1.7): Pre-fetch next segment TTS while current one plays — eliminates gaps between sections. // FEAT-CV-SPEED (v1.1.7): Speed control in toolbar (0.75×, 0.9×, 1×, 1.1×, 1.25×, 1.5×). Applies immediately, even mid-sentence. No DB changes. // UI-CV-NO-ICONS (v1.1.6): Removed all per-paragraph speaker icons from SCORM content. Toolbar-only UX — click Play in the toolbar to read all sections. Paragraph being read is highlighted with a blue tint and scrolled into view. No DB changes. // FIX-CV-AUTOPLAY (v1.1.5): Replaced HTMLAudioElement + audio.play() with Web AudioContext (decodeAudioData + BufferSource). AudioContext is unlocked during the user click gesture; BufferSource.start() then works from async XHR callbacks without hitting browser autoplay policy. Pause/resume uses BufferSource offset tracking so mid-segment position is preserved. // UI-CV-VOICES (v1.1.5): Reordered voice dropdown — males first (Charon, Fenrir, Orus, Puck) then females (Aoede, Kore, Leda, Zephyr). // UI-CV-DROPDOWN (v1.1.5): Widened voice/language dropdowns from max-width:130px to min-width:200px so full voice descriptions are visible. // FIX-CV-RISE-DETECT (v1.1.0): Fixed "No text sections found" on SCORM packages where the outer shell has 151–500 chars of body text (script blocks, a11y labels, status divs). Root cause: resolveContentDoc() had a premature early-return when outerDoc bodyText > 300 — it returned the shell doc immediately without ever checking whether a child iframe held the actual Rise 360 lesson. waitForContent() only called resolveContentDoc() when bodyText <= 150, so shells with 151-499 chars of text bypassed the iframe-detection entirely and passed the wrong document to onContentReady. extractSegments found zero lesson elements and showed "No text sections found". Fix: (1) resolveContentDoc() now ALWAYS checks child iframes first — the > 300 short-circuit is removed entirely; child iframes are preferred if any has > 100 chars of text. (2) waitForContent() now calls resolveContentDoc() on every tick BEFORE the body-text threshold check, not conditionally. No DB schema changes. // FEAT-CV-TEACHER-LANG (v1.0.8): Teacher language settings per course. New local_chirpvoice_course_settings DB table. Teachers with moodle/course:manageactivities can visit course_settings.php to restrict which languages appear in the voiceover toolbar for their students. The course-level list is always a subset of the admin-allowed list (privilege escalation impossible). lib.php looks up course settings and passes effective allowed languages to JS; ajax.php validates the requested language against course-level allowed list. A gear icon appears in the toolbar for teachers linking directly to course_settings.php. All languages cost 3 credits per paragraph — no per-language pricing difference. DB: new local_chirpvoice_course_settings table (courseid UNIQUE, allowedlanguages TEXT, timecreated, timemodified). Savepoint 2026060500009. // FIX-CV-AUDIT-NESTED (v1.0.7): Fixed nested-iframe detection timing. resolveContentDoc() now called on every poll tick inside waitForContent() instead of once at tryAccess() time — catches child iframe the moment Rise 360 renders. // FIX-CV-AUDIT (v1.0.6): Nav label blocking, Labeled Graphic support, text deduplication, nested iframe detection, blob URL revoke. No further DB schema changes beyond v1.0.8 table.
$plugin->supported = [400, 500];     // Moodle 4.0 to 5.x
